{#
  Default Jinja2 template for formatting a batch of log records for an AI model.
  Variables available:
  - logs: A list of log record dictionaries. Each dictionary contains keys like:
    - timestamp
    - levelname
    - message
    - pathname
    - funcName
    - lineno
    - exception_info (if any)
    - stack_info (if any)
    - extras (if any)
#}
Analyze the following batch of application log records. Identify any potential issues, errors, or noteworthy patterns.
Provide a concise summary of your findings. If there are critical errors, highlight them.

Log Batch ({{ logs|length }} records):
==================================================

{% for log_entry in logs %}
Timestamp: {{ log_entry.timestamp }}
Level:     {{ log_entry.levelname }}
Logger:    {{ log_entry.name }}
Message:   {{ log_entry.message }}
{% if log_entry.pathname %}Source:    {{ log_entry.pathname }}:{{ log_entry.lineno }} (in {{ log_entry.funcName }}){% endif %}
{% if log_entry.exception_info %}
Exception Info:
{{ log_entry.exception_info|indent(2, true) }}
{% endif %}
{% if log_entry.stack_info %}
Stack Info:
{{ log_entry.stack_info|indent(2, true) }}
{% endif %}
{% if log_entry.extras %}
Extra Data: {{ log_entry.extras|tojson }}
{% endif %}
--------------------------------------------------
{% endfor %}

End of Log Batch.

AI Analysis Summary:
